From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] halium: bind /cache when the mountpoint exists but is unmounted

The cache bind-mount was guarded by "[ ! -e ${mount_root}/cache ]", which is
false on every GSI, because a GSI ships /cache as an empty directory. So the
bind never happened on any system-as-root port and /android/cache was left
unmounted.

That is harmless until the device's vendor fstab has a cache entry the Android
container cannot satisfy. On the Unihertz Titan Pocket it cannot, init treats
it as fatal, and the phone bootloops:

  libfs_mgr: mke2fs returned 256
  libfs_mgr: failed to format cache
  libfs_mgr: failed to mount cache: invalid argument

Also note pre-start.sh only strips mount_all from the container's init rc on the
LEGACY layout - the sed sits in the "else" branch of "if [ -e /android/init ]" -
so on a GSI the container really does run fs_mgr itself. Fixing that is a
separate question; providing /cache is correct regardless, and is what UBports
do in their own Titan Pocket/Slim adaptation.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/scripts/halium
+++ b/scripts/halium
@@ -198,13 +198,35 @@
 		mount $path ${mount_root}/$2 -t $3 -o $mount_option_cleaned
 	done
 
-	# Provide a bind mount from /cache to /userdata/cache on systems without a dedicated cache partition
-	if [ ! -e ${mount_root}/cache ]; then
+	# Provide a bind mount from /cache to /userdata/cache on systems without a
+	# dedicated cache partition - and also when the mountpoint exists but
+	# nothing is mounted on it, which is the case on EVERY GSI. A GSI ships
+	# /cache as an empty directory (inode 17, mode 0770 system:cache in
+	# halium-luneos-16.0-20260910-1-halium_arm64), so "! -e" is false, the bind
+	# was skipped, and /android/cache was left unmounted.
+	#
+	# The Android container's init then runs mount_all over the vendor fstab and
+	# tries to mount the real cache partition itself. On the Unihertz Titan
+	# Pocket that cannot be satisfied and init treats it as fatal, so the phone
+	# reboots in a loop with
+	#
+	#   libfs_mgr: mke2fs returned 256
+	#   libfs_mgr: failed to format cache
+	#   libfs_mgr: failed to mount cache: invalid argument
+	#
+	# UBports carry exactly this extra test in their Titan Pocket/Slim port.
+	# Note the surrounding spaces in the /proc/mounts match: the field is a
+	# whole mountpoint, and without them this also matches e.g. /android/cachefs.
+	#
+	# mkdir needs -p now: in the GSI case the directory already exists, and a
+	# plain mkdir would fail and leave the bind undone.
+	if [ ! -e ${mount_root}/cache ] || ! grep -q " ${mount_root}/cache " /proc/mounts; then
 		if [ ! -d ${real_userdata}/cache ]; then
 			mkdir ${real_userdata}/cache
 		fi
-		mkdir ${mount_root}/cache
+		mkdir -p ${mount_root}/cache
 		mount -o bind ${real_userdata}/cache ${mount_root}/cache
+		tell_kmsg "bound ${real_userdata}/cache to ${mount_root}/cache"
 	fi
 
 	# Create an appropriate symlink for vendor files
